k first.", "raw_text": {"text": "Dear young x posters looking for a quick \u201cgotcha\u201d to post. \n\nThink first.", "display_text_range": [0, 73], "facets": []}, "author": {"screen_name": "unclebobmartin", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin", "id": "9505092", "followers": 282563, "following": 366, "likes": 7447, "media_count": 2721, "statuses": 46580, "name": "Uncle Bob Martin", "description": "Software Craftsman", "raw_description": {"text": "Software Craftsman", "facets": []}, "location": "iPhone: 56.802658,9.868149", "banner_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/9505092/1774556131", "avatar_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2037262183751704577/54AiU968_200x200.jpg", "joined": "Wed Oct 17 19:03:34 +0000 2007", "protected": false, "website": {"url": "http://cleancoder.com", "display_url": "cleancoder.com"}, "verification": {"verified": true, "verified_at": null, "type": "individual"}, "type": "profile"}, "replies": 32, "reposts": 3, "likes": 205, "bookmarks": 4, "quotes": 5, "embed_card": "tweet", "created_at": "Tue Aug 18 11:47:54 +0000 2026", "created_timestamp": 1787053674, "views": 25763, "is_note_tweet": false, "community_note": null, "lang": "en", "replying_to": null, "media": {}, "provider": "twitter", "reposted_by": null}, {"type": "status", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin/status/2089483721455874503", "id": "2089483721455874503", "text": "The Squad...", "raw_text": {"text": "The Squad... https://t.co/Ndf6lW7H3h", "display_text_range": [0, 12], "facets": [{"type": "media", "indices": [13, 36], "id": "2089483672860643328", "display": "pic.x.com/Ndf6lW7H3h", "original": "https://t.co/Ndf6lW7H3h", "replacement": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin/status/2089483721455874503/photo/1"}]}, "author": {"screen_name": "unclebobmartin", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin", "id": "9505092", "followers": 282563, "following": 366, "likes": 7447, "media_count": 2721, "statuses": 46580, "name": "Uncle Bob Martin", "description": "Software Craftsman", "raw_description": {"text": "Software Craftsman", "facets": []}, "location": "iPhone: 56.802658,9.868149", "banner_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/9505092/1774556131", "avatar_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2037262183751704577/54AiU968_200x200.jpg", "joined": "Wed Oct 17 19:03:34 +0000 2007", "protected": false, "website": {"url": "http://cleancoder.com", "display_url": "cleancoder.com"}, "verification": {"verified": true, "verified_at": null, "type": "individual"}, "type": "profile"}, "replies": 34, "reposts": 13, "likes": 557, "bookmarks": 296, "quotes": 1, "embed_card": "summary_large_image", "created_at": "Mon Aug 17 22:45:14 +0000 2026", "created_timestamp": 1787006714, "possibly_sensitive": false, "views": 65847, "is_note_tweet": false, "community_note": null, "lang": "en", "replying_to": null, "media": {"all": [{"type": "photo", "id": "2089483672860643328", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HP9WVHTWUAATBy5.jpg?name=orig", "width": 1372, "height": 981}], "photos": [{"type": "photo", "id": "2089483672860643328", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HP9WVHTWUAATBy5.jpg?name=orig", "width": 1372, "height": 981}]}, "provider": "twitter", "reposted_by": null}, {"type": "status", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin/status/2089449442089025936", "id": "2089449442089025936", "text": "I ran the negative test experiment.  Interesting.   repo below.\n\nAbstract written by grok:\n\nWe wrote Hunt the Wumpus eight times from empty: four testing disciplines, with and without forcing CRAP below 4. Every run passed the same 25 acceptance cases. The programs were not the same. Discipline changed both the unit suite and the shape of the source. Three laws grew a layered immutable hunt; test-last left a small program with a few fat functions; bundling named every function and kept the domain off stdout; none produced a BASIC-style listing with no unit tests. CRAP then split functions and added tests until every score was under 4. It raised coverage (and invented a whole suite when there had been none) and made every program harder to read. It did not improve design. Mutation, run afterward against each frozen tree, wrote a second suite aimed at operators, not a different Wumpus. Acceptance never distinguished any of this.\n\nhttps://github.com/unclebob/negative-test-experiment", "raw_text": {"text": "I ran the negative test experiment.  Interesting.   repo below.\n\nAbstract written by grok:\n\nWe wrote Hunt the Wumpus eight times from empty: four testing disciplines, with and without forcing CRAP below 4. Every run passed the same 25 acceptance cases. The programs were not the same. Discipline changed both the unit suite and the shape of the source. Three laws grew a layered immutable hunt; test-last left a small program with a few fat functions; bundling named every function and kept the domain off stdout; none produced a BASIC-style listing with no unit tests. CRAP then split functions and added tests until every score was under 4. It raised coverage (and invented a whole suite when there had been none) and made every program harder to read. It did not improve design. Mutation, run afterward against each frozen tree, wrote a second suite aimed at operators, not a different Wumpus. Acceptance never distinguished any of this.\n\nhttps://t.co/2Zd0w7Pm8g", "display_text_range": [0, 965], "facets": [{"type": "url", "indices": [942, 965], "original": "https://t.co/2Zd0w7Pm8g", "replacement": "https://github.com/unclebob/negative-test-experiment", "display": "github.com/unclebob/negat\u2026"}]}, "author": {"screen_name": "unclebobmartin", "url": "https://x.com/unclebobmartin", "id": "9505092", "followers": 282563, "following": 366, "likes": 7447, "media_count": 2721, "statuses": 46580, "name": "Uncle Bob Martin", "description": "Software Craftsman", "raw_description": {"text": "Software Craftsman", "facets": []}, "location": "iPhone: 56.802658,9.868149", "banner_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/9505092/